  "body": "It's does not appear to be specified anywhere in the spec (or if it is it's obscure enough that I couldn't locate it) whether or not the concept of focus as discussed in the algorithm for determining the [\"Currently Focused Area of a Top Level Browsing Context\"](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#currently-focused-area-of-a-top-level-browsing-context) or the [\"Has Focus Steps\"](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#has-focus-steps) should take into account whether or not the underlying OS has given the UA in focus. As such it seems like a valid interpretation of the text for the UA to indicate return `document.hasFocus() == true` for the last focused document in the UA whether or not the UA itself currently has system-level focus.\r\n\r\nTo be clear, it appears that no UAs actually interpret the spec that way, and it definitely feels as though system-level focus is what's intended to be evaluated. It was an [issue that came up during development of the WebXR spec](https://github.com/immersive-web/webxr/issues/747), however, so it felt worthwhile to ask for either a clarification to the spec text or to be directed to existing text which clarifies what the concept of focus encompasses.\r\n\r\nThank you!",
